  "units": [
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.SS1.p1.1",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source_line": 1911,
      "raw_html_sha256": "8b460c7c667c6dfd5362b5a0955a4206be5fb6d031879a9cb63042bcab629195",
      "raw_html_bytes": 1161,
      "mathematical_text": "Both identities below are instances of the Poisson integral formula for the unit ball of \\mathbb{R}^{n}, applied at the point re_{1} to the harmonic functions 1 and y\\mapsto y_{1}.",
      "raw_html": "<p id=\"A1.SS1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Both identities below are instances of the Poisson integral formula for the\nunit ball of <math id=\"A1.SS1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{R}^{n}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, applied at the point <math id=\"A1.SS1.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"re_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">re_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the harmonic\nfunctions <math id=\"A1.SS1.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"A1.SS1.p1.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"y\\mapsto y_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y\\mapsto y_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.Thmtheorem1",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "source_line": 1915,
      "raw_html_sha256": "a690970aa5eb55e4b2d6c1dc76f0bd79cec1c70cc90d6842dfb27bcec8788c55",
      "raw_html_bytes": 4165,
      "mathematical_text": "Lemma A.1 (Spherical Poisson identities).",
      "raw_html": "<div id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1\" class=\"ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma\">\n<h6 class=\"ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem\"><span id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.2\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.3\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\"> </span>(<span id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.4\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_bold\">Spherical Poisson identities).</span></h6>\n<div id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n<p id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Let <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\\geq 2\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\zeta=(\\zeta_{1},\\dots,\\zeta_{n})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\zeta=(\\zeta_{1},\\dots,\\zeta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniform random point on\n<math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U=\\zeta_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=\\zeta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be its first coordinate., where <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\\geq 3\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor every <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0&lt;r&lt;1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;r&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>\n<table id=\"A1.E12\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"A1.E12.m1\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{E}\\left[(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{1}{1-r^{2}},\\qquad\\mathbb{E}\\left[U(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{r}{1-r^{2}}.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace=\"0em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{E}\\left[(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{1}{1-r^{2}},\\qquad\\mathbb{E}\\left[U(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{r}{1-r^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source_line": 1918,
      "raw_html_sha256": "8be8e992147f6c3a912952768481127676b2389f470920e3d00b345bf6d7d785",
      "raw_html_bytes": 1978,
      "mathematical_text": "Let n\\geq 2, and \\zeta=(\\zeta_{1},\\dots,\\zeta_{n}) be a uniform random point on \\mathbb{S}^{n-1}, and let U=\\zeta_{1} be its first coordinate., where n\\geq 3. For every 0<r<1,",
      "raw_html": "<p id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Let <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\\geq 2\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\zeta=(\\zeta_{1},\\dots,\\zeta_{n})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\zeta=(\\zeta_{1},\\dots,\\zeta_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be a uniform random point on\n<math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"U=\\zeta_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U=\\zeta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be its first coordinate., where <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"n\\geq 3\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n\\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.\nFor every <math id=\"A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0&lt;r&lt;1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;r&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.E12",
      "kind": "display",
      "source_line": 1921,
      "raw_html_sha256": "67ec35b50f20360b55e05f1a9e1880cfb6c737fdc1a64178a048c824d5eee5bb",
      "raw_html_bytes": 1722,
      "mathematical_text": "\\mathbb{E}\\left[(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{1}{1-r^{2}},\\qquad\\mathbb{E}\\left[U(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{r}{1-r^{2}}.",
      "raw_html": "<table id=\"A1.E12\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"A1.E12.m1\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{E}\\left[(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{1}{1-r^{2}},\\qquad\\mathbb{E}\\left[U(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{r}{1-r^{2}}.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace=\"0em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{E}\\left[(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{1}{1-r^{2}},\\qquad\\mathbb{E}\\left[U(1+r^{2}-2rU)^{-n/2}\\right]=\\frac{r}{1-r^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.SS1.p2.1",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source_line": 1934,
      "raw_html_sha256": "b28926f6798dad00ed7f968c74820b19613ac9a456b98be8fc7b2bec08040145",
      "raw_html_bytes": 1016,
      "mathematical_text": "Let \\sigma be normalized surface measure on \\mathbb{S}^{n-1}. By the Poisson representation formula [5, Theorem 1.21], every function h harmonic on the unit ball and continuous on its closure satisfies",
      "raw_html": "<p id=\"A1.SS1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"A1.SS1.p2.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Let <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\sigma\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be normalized surface measure on <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nBy the Poisson representation formula\n<cite class=\"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite\">[<a href=\"#bib.bib24\" title=\"\" class=\"ltx_ref\">5</a>, Theorem 1.21]</cite>,\nevery function <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"h\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h</annotation></semantics></math> harmonic on the unit ball and continuous\non its closure satisfies</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.Ex31",
      "kind": "display",
      "source_line": 1939,
      "raw_html_sha256": "e12c9ebc4fe84429ec79ecce77749a072ee90fad0d616dd4bbfedeb5ea08d6bc",
      "raw_html_bytes": 1770,
      "mathematical_text": "h(a)=\\int_{\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}}h(u)\\frac{1-\\|a\\|^{2}}{\\|u-a\\|^{n}}\\,d\\sigma(u),\\qquad\\|a\\|<1.",
      "raw_html": "<table id=\"A1.Ex31\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"A1.Ex31.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"h(a)=\\int_{\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}}h(u)\\frac{1-\\|a\\|^{2}}{\\|u-a\\|^{n}}\\,d\\sigma(u),\\qquad\\|a\\|&lt;1.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.111em\">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>𝕊</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace=\"0em\">𝑑</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(a)=\\int_{\\mathbb{S}^{n-1}}h(u)\\frac{1-\\|a\\|^{2}}{\\|u-a\\|^{n}}\\,d\\sigma(u),\\qquad\\|a\\|&lt;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "region": "A1.SS1",
      "anchor": "A1.SS1.p2.2",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source_line": 1946,
      "raw_html_sha256": "7c0a1e4b774fe2f75b73dd07dd4d81c0f6f779a3c2a3825381086342d892521e",
      "raw_html_bytes": 2174,
      "mathematical_text": "Apply this formula with a=re_{1} and, respectively, h(x)=1 and h(x)=x_{1}. Since \\|u-re_{1}\\|^{2}=1+r^{2}-2ru_{1}, the two applications prove the lemma after division by 1-r^{2}. ∎",
      "raw_html": "<p id=\"A1.SS1.p2.2\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"A1.SS1.p2.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Apply this formula with <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"a=re_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">a=re_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and, respectively,\n<math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"h(x)=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"h(x)=x_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(x)=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nSince <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m7\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\|u-re_{1}\\|^{2}=1+r^{2}-2ru_{1}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\|u-re_{1}\\|^{2}=1+r^{2}-2ru_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two applications prove the lemma\nafter division by <math id=\"A1.SS1.p2.m8\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"1-r^{2}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1-r^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.\n∎</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "region": "bib.bib24",
