      "mathematical_text": "[5] S. Axler, P. Bourdon, and R. Wade (2001) Harmonic function theory. Vol. 137, Springer Science & Business Media. Cited by: §A.1.",
      "raw_html": "<li id=\"bib.bib24\" class=\"ltx_bibitem ltx_bib_book\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_bib_key ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem\">[5]</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_bibblock\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_bib_author\">S. Axler, P. Bourdon, and R. Wade</span><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_bib_year\"> (2001)</span>\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_bibblock\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_bib_title\">Harmonic function theory</span>.\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_bibblock\">Vol. <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_bib_volume\">137</span>,  <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_bib_publisher\">Springer Science &amp; Business Media</span>.\n</span>\n<span class=\"ltx_bibblock ltx_bib_cited\">Cited by: <a href=\"#A1.SS1.p2.1.1\" title=\"Proof. ‣ A.1 Two Spherical Poisson Identities ‣ Appendix A Useful Facts ‣ On Complexity of Gaussian Sampling\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">§A.1</span></a>.\n</span></li>"
    }
